<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis De Geer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1587">1587</a>–<a href="/years/1652">1652</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Louis De Geer the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis De Geer was a Dutch-born merchant and industrialist who became the leading entrepreneur of 17th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Settling there in the 1620s, he developed the ironworks of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppland">Uppland</a>, brought in Walloon smiths, became the main arms supplier of the Swedish crown during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>, and was ennobled. He founded the Swedish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> Company in 1649.</p></div>
